  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <div class="faq">
    <h3>Does responding to Google reviews help SEO?</h3>
    <p>Google has not said that replies are a ranking factor. Its local ranking help page says more reviews and positive ratings can help local ranking, and that replies show you value feedback and can help your business stand out. Any direct ranking effect of replies is unconfirmed.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq">
    <h3>Should I put keywords in my review replies?</h3>
    <p>Google has not said that keywords in replies affect ranking, and we found no published test of it. Mention your type of business only where it reads naturally; replies are written for customers.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq">
    <h3>Does replying faster improve my ranking?</h3>
    <p>Google asks for timely replies but makes no ranking claim about speed. Customers do notice: in BrightLocal's 2026 survey, 81% expected a reply within a week.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq">
    <h3>Can replying to reviews hurt my profile?</h3>
    <p>A reply that breaks Google's content policies is not published, and offering incentives to change or remove reviews breaks Google's rules for merchants. Otherwise Google describes replies only in positive terms.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq" style="border:none">
    <h3>Is it worth replying to old reviews?</h3>
    <p>Google&#39;s help pages do not address the ranking effect of replying to old reviews. Customers still read them, so a specific reply to an old complaint that has since been fixed is useful to the next reader.</p>
  </div>

